# =============================================================================
# game-fixes: what never goes into the public repository.
#
# One file for the whole tree on purpose: a new game folder is protected the
# moment it is created, without anyone remembering to give it its own ignore
# file. The policy: crash evidence, notes about the owner's machines and game
# binaries never leave the machine they were made on. Only results are
# published: the fix or the mod, and how to use it.
#
# This file decides WHICH files are published. What is INSIDE the files that
# pass is checked by publish-check.py - run it before every push.
#
# Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth.
# =============================================================================

# --- local-only working material ---------------------------------------------
# Crash evidence, reports sent to developers, notes about the owner's machines,
# investigation journals, diagnostic helpers. These names are reserved for that
# purpose at every depth: do not name a source folder "local", "dumps",
# "bugreport" or "logs".
bugreport/
dumps/
local/
LOCAL-NOTES*.md
.publish-check.local
logs/
*.log

# Machine-local build hook of the Minecraft mods: where the game lives on this
# PC and what else to tidy up after an install.
build_local.py

# --- instructions for coding agents stay local -------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/

# --- crash data, wherever it turns up ----------------------------------------
# A memory dump holds game code and whatever else was in RAM at the time.
*.dmp
*.mdmp
*.hdmp
*.wer
*.etl
*.nv-gpudmp
CrashContext.runtime-xml

# --- game files: copyrighted, never ours to publish --------------------------
# Patched binaries and their backups live next to the game, not here.
*.exe
*.dll
*.pak
*.utoc
*.ucas
*.orig
*.bak
*.installed-before
*.before-*

# --- archives ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this repository is distributed as an archive; third-party resource
# packs and zipped dumps are the only archives that ever show up here.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz

# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
# The Minecraft mods are published as release downloads, not through git.
# Ignoring every .jar also keeps Minecraft and third-party mod jars out.
build/
*.class
*.jar

# --- python / node -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# --- editors, OS --------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- a repository of its own -------------------------------------------------
# Published separately as github.com/svareyko/ready-or-not-crash-fix and has its
# own ignore rules. Without this line "git add ." would swallow it as an
# embedded repository.
/ready-or-not/

# --- no publishable result yet -----------------------------------------------
# Open investigations: a cause is known or suspected, a verified fix is not.
# A folder leaves this list when it has something a player can use.
/mafia-2/
/cyberpunk-2077/

# --- the owner's personal Minecraft setup ------------------------------------
# Tooling around third-party resource packs and a deployment helper for a
# second PC. The mods themselves (minecraft/<mod>/) are published.
/minecraft/remote/
/minecraft/make-vanilla-overlay.py
/minecraft/patch-packs.py
